      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I run into this all the time. I would amend this request, though, by asking to append the player ID to the name, since that's useful info to have for free, and it's unique by definition.\n\nNot only is this an issue for code's reading of usernames, it's an issue for human reading of usernames. If I'm testing anything at all that lists players, then I have no way to differentiate various copies of myself.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-16T17:12:02.442Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Atm usernames are identical among all launched test clients. A toggle to append a number or random characters to a local client username would make testing username functionality in our behavior easier, and it would make testing hash based collections in the future udon 2 possible.",
